{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>These are the waters of Meribah.</b> They are the ones mentioned elsewhere. Pharaoh's astrologers saw these — that the savior of Israel would be stricken through water; therefore they decreed, ״כָּל הַבֵּן הַיִּלּוֹד הַיְאֹרָה תַּשְׁלִיכֻהוּ״ (Exodus 1) (Sanhedrin 101)." "<b>And He was sanctified in them.</b> For Moses and Aaron died on their account. When the Holy One, blessed be He, executes judgment upon His sanctified ones, He is feared and sanctified among mortals, and so it says, ״נוֹרָא אֱלֹהִים מִמִּקְדָּשֶׁיךָ״ (Psalms 68), and so it says, ״בִּקְרֹבַי אֶקָּדֵשׁ״ (Leviticus 10)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:43.687360409Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}